values ('b7d3e1a5-4c28-4f09-8b16-2e0a6c5d9f31', 'nutrition-for-health-and-performance', 'Nutrition for Health and Performance', 'This course teaches nutrition as an applied health and performance science for kinesiology students. Learners examine energy metabolism, macronutrients, micronutrients, hydration, nutrient timing, supplements, body composition, weight management, special populations, and eating-disorder risk while practicing evidence-based, ethical, culturally responsive communication. The course emphasizes practical decision-making: assess context, interpret evidence, protect health, support training adaptation, and know when referral is required.');

